Modifications
-------------

Changed between 2026-05 and 2026-10, to record a per-point confidence channel
set while the SLAM runs rather than reconstructing one afterwards, and to fix
problems met on our recordings. GPL-2.0 section 2(a) requires changed files to
say so. Compared against upstream at the time of writing:

NEW FILE

  src/range_image.hpp     Within-scan "detachment" channels, computed on the
                          raw organised scan before any downsampling:
                          range_detach, range_edge, int_detach, ring_rough.
                          Each point's range is extrapolated along its detector
                          row from three cells on either side, skipping the
                          immediate neighbours, and the residual is normalised
                          by range. Nothing upstream corresponds to this.

CHANGED FILES

  src/voxelslam.cpp       The largest change.
                          - Per-point and per-scan confidence values recorded
                            from the IEKF frontend and the local bundle
                            adjustment, and written with each saved scan.
                          - SaveFields/* parameters to choose which channels
                            are written.
                          - FIX, off-by-one in the plane gate: upstream sets
                            `min_point << 5, 5, 5, 5`, a fixed four entries,
                            while plane_judge() indexes it by layer over the
                            inclusive range 0..max_layer. With max_layer = 4 the
                            deepest layer read past the end of the vector. It is
                            now sized max_layer+1, with LocalBA/min_point_deepest
                            to set the deepest layer explicitly.
                          - save_pose() no longer dereferences an empty buffer.

  src/voxel_map.hpp       - pointVar carries the confidence fields (balm_res,
                            ekf_res, plane_quality, cell_id, reflectivity,
                            ambient, ring, scan_time, the family-B channels)
                            and the per-voxel statistics obs_count,
                            view_diversity and temp_consistency, accumulated
                            incrementally as scans are inserted.
                          - a leaf query used when the scans are merged.

  src/tools.hpp           - The confidence fields added to the point struct and
                            registered with PCL, so they survive into the saved
                            clouds.
                          - CHANGED BEHAVIOUR, down_sampling_voxel() takes an
                            `average_xyz` flag. Upstream always replaces the
                            points in a voxel with their running centroid. With
                            the flag false the first point in the voxel is kept
                            instead, so every saved point is a real measurement
                            rather than an average of several. Default true,
                            which is upstream's behaviour.

  src/feature_point.hpp   - Sensor handlers fill the new fields.
                          - The Hesai handler rebuilds an organised range image
                            from ring index and azimuth, which that driver does
                            not provide, so the within-scan channels exist for
                            it too.

  src/ekf_imu.hpp         FIX: motion_blur() returns bool instead of calling
                          exit(0) when a scan's timestamps regress against the
                          previous scan. A recording stall used to abort the
                          whole run; the affected scan is now skipped.

  src/voxelslam.hpp       Plumbing for the above.

  src/loop_refine.hpp     Uses PointType rather than pcl::PointXYZINormal when
                          reading the nearest target point, so the normal
                          fields are the ones this build actually stores.

  scripts/                global_pcd_converter.py merges the saved scans into
                          one global cloud using the final trajectory and
                          completes the per-voxel statistics over the session.
                          Not part of upstream Voxel-SLAM.

  CMakeLists.txt          - Raises the Boost.MPL vector and list limits to 30.
                          The extended point type carries 23 registered fields,
                          and PCL's field list is built with Boost.MPL, whose
                          containers default to 20; going over that fails as
                          "no type named 'type' in struct pcl::traits::fieldList".
                          - Adds -g to keep line numbers in backtraces, and
                          drops the livox_ros_driver dependency, which we do
                          not use.

  launch/, config/        Settings for the sensors used in our experiments:
                          vxlm_ouster.launch and ouster.yaml retargeted at our
                          platform's topics, and vxlm_oxford_spires.launch with
                          oxford_spires_ds02.yaml added for the Hesai QT64 of
                          the Oxford Spires dataset. config/hesai.yaml is
                          upstream and unchanged.

UNCHANGED

  src/BTC.cpp, src/BTC.h, src/preintegration.hpp are upstream as published.

Everything not listed above is upstream Voxel-SLAM.


Scope
-----

The GPL covers this directory. The rest of this repository -- the labelling,
feature and evaluation code under ../scripts -- is a separate work that reads
the files this SLAM writes. It does not link against or include any part of
Voxel-SLAM, and is distributed alongside it as an aggregate, which GPL-2.0
section 2 permits. See the top-level README for its licence.
